{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining\nthe contributions specified by the requirements applicable to that subject and\nits inputs. A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and\ndefine which sources it contributes and when. The harness MUST include every\napplicable contribution, deduplicate identical selections, and report\nunresolvable mandatory inputs before inference. The complete set MUST be supplied\nin the initial model request.\nGenerated output under project-root `evidence/`, including symlink aliases, MUST\nbe omitted from mandatory inputs when the default exclusion applies. An explicit\nworkspace allow MUST permit those selections; an explicit disallow MUST abort\nunder {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate for `requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs`. This is based on the supplied test text only. I did not request any implementation source.\n\n**Obligations and the tests that cover them**\n\n1. **Combine every applicable contribution.**\n   - `bundle_combines_direct_references_terms_and_current_existing_selectors` checks these contributions:\n     - the subject's own declaration;\n     - directly cited requirements, which are included;\n     - distant requirements, which are excluded;\n     - an example citing the subject;\n     - a `{test}` item, which is included;\n     - an `{impl}` item, which is excluded;\n     - the terms used.\n   - It also checks that earlier evidence inputs and judgments are not carried forward.\n   - `only_edges_leaving_the_subject_contribute_inputs` checks both directions of the edges:\n     - the subject's outgoing cites and test items are included;\n     - an incoming citer or `{impl}` parent is not;\n     - the example and parent subjects get the contributions that apply to them.\n   - `anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs` and `test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node` check anchor contributions: a whole file, and only the selected node.\n   - `references_contribute_their_owning_outline_nodes` checks markdown sections, plain-text files and `{fixme}` metadata.\n   - `mandatory_git_inputs_require_staging_declarations_sources_and_terms` checks that staged declarations, sources and terms contribute.\n   - `citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once` and `site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site` check the citation-review and site-review input sets.\n\n2. **Deduplicate identical selections.**\n   - `citation_review_inputs_combine_item_declarations_terms_and_built_ins_once` repeats a cite, a shared term and a built-in text. It asserts exactly one of each and a total of 5 inputs.\n   - `anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs` anchors both `:impl:` and `:test:` to the same file. It asserts the exact input list, so that file appears once.\n   - The bundle test's two mutually referencing terms yield exactly 2 definitions.\n   - `implementation_discovery_has_no_text_or_evidence_until_the_model_requests_a_read` checks that a later read of an already delivered item is recorded once.\n\n3. **Report unresolvable mandatory inputs before inference.**\n   - These tests check preparation aborts with `PermissionDenied`, naming the path:\n     - `disallowed_mandatory_inputs_abort_preparation`;\n     - `mandatory_inputs_outside_the_project_still_abort`;\n     - `unreadable_or_denied_anchors_fail_before_inference`, which also covers a missing file and a missing node.\n   - `unresolvable_mandatory_inputs_fail_before_any_model_request` runs the CLI against a listener that must never be contacted. It asserts a nonzero exit, that stderr names the path, and that the evidence file is unchanged.\n   - `unresolvable_earlier_inputs_do_not_block_reassessment` confirms that stale recorded inputs are not mandatory.\n\n4. **Supply the complete set in the initial request.**\n   - `citation_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_the_item_and_citations` checks that the first prompt contains the item hash, the cited requirement text and the built-in text.\n   - `site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site` compares the subject message to the expected fill-in of the mandatory inputs.\n   - `test_anchors_supply_only_the_selected_node` checks the prompt contains the anchored node and not the sibling.\n   - The CLI tests `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free` and `implementation_discovery_has_no_text_or_evidence_until_the_model_requests_a_read` assert the first HTTP request body contains the requirement, the definition and the test.\n\n5. **Generated `evidence/` output.**\n   - `generated_evidence_anchors_are_omitted_unless_allowed_and_abort_when_disallowed` checks four cases:\n     - the default exclusion omits an `evidence/` anchor without aborting;\n     - a symlink alias into `evidence/` is omitted (Unix only);\n     - an explicit allow includes the anchor;\n     - an explicit disallow aborts with `PermissionDenied`.\n   - `generated_evidence_references_are_omitted_by_default` checks references found under `evidence/` are not contributed, and that an allow does not change that.\n\n**Delegated obligations**\n\n- The requirement that a contributing requirement cite this one and define its sources is carried by those requirements' own text, not by tests here.\n- Writing no evidence, emitting no evidence JSON, usage records and batch behaviour belong to `requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`, which is cited context. The tests here still show the abort happens before any model request and that the evidence file is unchanged.\n\n**Gaps and acknowledgments**\n\nI found no untested obligation and no assertion that contradicts the text. All the cited tests carry `{test}` references. No acknowledgments apply.",
